#op: decompile
Decompile turns a normal-form lineage back into version files. It expresses
exactly the lenses the compiler produces: mappings that move, drop, orelse,
remap and each. A lens that computes a value is outside that, and Decompile
refuses it rather than approximate.
-- lineage.cue --
name: "ship"
schemas: {
	"0": {
		"0": {
			schema: {
				a: string
			}
		}
	}
	"1": {
		"0": {
			schema: {
				a: string
				n: int
			}
		}
	}
}
lenses: {
	"0.0->1.0": {
		input: _
		result: {
			a: input.a
			n: len(input.a)
		}
	}
	"1.0->0.0": {
		input: _
		result: {
			a: input.a
		}
	}
}
-- out/json --
{
  "diagnostics": [
    {
      "code": "E0356",
      "severity": "error",
      "headline": "lens 0.0->1.0 is outside the authoring form: n is computed",
      "primary": {
        "file": "lineage.cue",
        "line": 1,
        "col": 1,
        "origin": "user"
      },
      "help": [
        "the authoring form expresses the lenses Compile produces: mappings that move, drop, orelse, remap and each"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "errors": 1,
    "warnings": 0,
    "notes": 0
  }
}
-- out/text --
error[E0356]: lens 0.0->1.0 is outside the authoring form: n is computed
 --> lineage.cue:1:1
  |
1 | name: "ship"
  | ^^^^
  |
